Orange Pi 4 Pro — headless LTS kernel
===================================

Linux 6.18 LTS with the pinned Xunlong A733 BSP, adapted for a minimal
wired server running Debian 13 from NVMe. This is an independent port,
not an official Orange Pi image or upstream board-support claim.

The optional eMMC controller is disabled: no module is available to debug
or qualify it. SD carries the existing vendor firmware and boot files;
NVMe carries the operating system. Graphics, NPU and wireless are outside
the qualified headless configuration. Future kernel series use separate
branches; no 7.x branch is currently maintained here.

Friday 21:17 AEST CI verifies the latest signed official 6.18 stable tag,
merges it into a candidate, builds in a pinned offline container, and
publishes an immutable candidate release with corresponding source.
Conflicts, build errors and publication failures fail the workflow and
open an issue; GitHub notification email delivery has been confirmed.
Vendor BSP changes require review and are never imported automatically.

Enrolled boards pull the 6.18 release feed over HTTPS. Each candidate is
checked and staged alongside the current kernel, then booted once under
the hardware watchdog. Only local health checks promote it. Incomplete
boots select the previous good set, then the preserved original recovery
kernel. CI publishes candidates; it does not connect to the LAN.
Kernel rollback does not restore shared root data or recover SD failure.

Build commands, supported hardware and qualification evidence:
  scripts/orangepi/README
Update policy, provenance and CI:
  scripts/orangepi/MAINTENANCE.md
Licence and corresponding upstream documentation:
  COPYING and Documentation/
